  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1243 PM MDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nThursday, drier air is forecast to move into the interior sections \nand it will likely be dry over the higher terrain. the best chance \nof any showers will be over the far southeastern plains during the \nlate afternoon and evening time period. Temperatures will be \nseasonable this day. Marginal critical fire weather conditions will \nbe possible over the interior mtns due to single digit min RH \nvalues and breezy conditions. \n\nFriday is expected to be mainly dry and much warmer, with mid 90s \nmost of plains and mid 80s valleys. It will be much drier over the \ninterior  and fire weather concerns will continua over the interior \nmtns (Although RH values will be a bit higher than Thursdays values).\n\nWeekend...Saturday will be cooler than Sunday (Mid 80s vs Low 90s). \nScattered storms are expected each day in the mtns with isolated \nover the plains. \n\nFor early next week, statistical guidance still shows quite a bit of \nvariability, but overall it shows a cooling trend with a better \nchance of showers and thunderstorms over the region. The \nvariability is likely due in part to the timing of a cool front \nwhich is forecast to come down the plains during the ~Tuesday-ish \ntime frame. \\/Hodanish",
